cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or analysis pipeline, please cite this repository and the associated publication."
title: "RPDindex-Based Aircraft-Engine RUL Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Righi"
    given-names: "Marco"
    affiliation: "Institute of Clinical Physiology, National Research Council of Italy (CNR-IFC), Massa, Italy; Department of Computer Science, University of Pisa, Pisa, Italy"
version: 1.0.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python analysis pipeline for evaluating RPDindex-based local and
  global degradation indicators and their use in remaining useful life (RUL)
  prediction for aircraft engines using the C-MAPSS-derived Predictive
  Maintenance Aircraft Engine dataset. The repository includes data integrity
  checks, RPD trajectory computation, statistical validation, RUL model
  training and validation, blind test prediction, evaluation, and manuscript
  figure generation.
keywords:
  - "RPDindex"
  - "remaining useful life"
  - "RUL prediction"
  - "predictive maintenance"
  - "aircraft engines"
  - "C-MAPSS"
  - "degradation indicators"
  - "reliability engineering"
  - "prognostics"
